{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Editor-server >30s attribution follow-up (rebar-debug Stage 3, 2026-08-14): run 31798375024 assigned 35.06s to setup of test_server_binds_loopback_only, but focused exact-test and whole-module runs remain subsecond/2.44s, and prior RCA cryptic-damp-panda recorded targeted edit_workflow phase instrumentation with a maximum of 3.927ms. The leading new hypothesis was pytest tmp_path numbered-directory scanning late in an xdist worker. A discriminating local APFS microbenchmark invoked pytest make_numbered_dir 30 times in roots containing 0, 4,000, and 10,000 sibling directories: median 0.125ms, 1.328ms, and 3.136ms (p95 0.141/1.458/3.319ms). This rejects retained tmp_path siblings as the mechanism by over four orders of magnitude. Pytest setup ordering confirms the reported phase includes all autouse fixtures plus tmp_path and _server, so the duration record is not an intrinsic individual-test call measurement. Combined with the prior 3.927ms server trace and the exact-test reproduction, the parsimonious attribution is transient macOS worker/process starvation under suite-wide subprocess/APFS contention, recorded against this setup phase rather than 35s of editor behavior. No test/fixture remediation is justified from this one sample; retain the test unchanged and watch future genuine Verify runs. No observability change is needed unless the setup phase recurs >30s after Pandoc subprocess load is reduced."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786712233331309001,"uuid":"a30095ce-c358-4b6d-89fc-81a55a820ecc"}